---
description: >-
  Two ways of naming a typed participant used side by side: an inline
  `"alias"` field inside the `@{...}` metadata (participant A), and the
  external `as` keyword (participant B), plus a plain typed participant with
  no alias (participant C).
config:
  look: classic
  sequence:
    diagramMarginX: 50
    diagramMarginY: 10
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant A@{ "type" : "boundary", "alias": "Service A" }
  participant B@{ "type" : "control" } as Service B
  participant C@{ "type" : "database" }
  A ->> B: Request
  B ->> C: Query
  C -->> B: Data
  B -->> A: Response
